  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-25T06:33:28.403Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Verified on both SDK versions:\nlatest VRCSDK3-WORLD-2021.03.22.18.27_Public\nand VRCSDK3-WORLD-2021.01.19.07.28_Public\n\nWhile trying to workaround the while loop bug, I discovered that \"Set Variable\" nodes are completely ignored when their input is shared with another Set Variable node elsewhere in the graph.\nIn the following program, I do some math to produce a \"true\" value which I assign to a variable. I check if the variable is true, then I set the variable to false, then I set the variable to an expression which should evaluate to true. However, the variable is simply set to false and the subsequent \"set variable\" is ignored.\nUdonFlat doesn't do a good job of illustrating the issue in this case, because it sees that the variable is set to a constant and optimizes it out, but the flat program is visible in the following scerenshot.\nI added a second screenshot with a more complicated (false==true) expression to force it to generate the variable assignment in the UdonFlat program.\nHere is the graph asset:\nhttps://gist.githubusercontent.com/lyuma/7da98ef4c77e80a44b3d4d1a8adca9ee/raw/2e667350cccf9b144a67d6594b1d8cb9ffd4f4ba/IfStatementWrong.asset",
